     "ParticipantRole": "CLINICIAN"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-1",
    "Content": "Thanks. I've been pretty nervous about the results.",
    "BeginAudioTime": 4.72,
    "EndAudioTime": 8.05,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "PATIENT"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-2",
    "Content": "That's completely understandable. So, we got the biopsy results back from your colonoscopy.",
    "BeginAudioTime": 8.65,
    "EndAudioTime": 14.53,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "CLINICIAN"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-3",
    "Content": "Okay.",
    "BeginAudioTime": 15.13,
    "EndAudioTime": 15.43,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "PATIENT"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-4",
    "Content": "The sample from the growth in your sigmoid colon showed what we call an adenocarcinoma.",
    "BeginAudioTime": 16.03,
    "EndAudioTime": 21.63,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "CLINICIAN"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-5",
    "Content": "That's a type of cancer that starts in the gland cells lining the colon.",
    "BeginAudioTime": 22.23,
    "EndAudioTime": 27.03,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "CLINICIAN"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-6",
    "Content": "Is it bad? Has it spread?",
    "BeginAudioTime": 27.63,
    "EndAudioTime": 29.58,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "PATIENT"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-7",
    "Content": "The biopsy alone can't tell us that. We'll do a CT scan of your chest, abdomen and pelvis to stage it.",
    "BeginAudioTime": 30.18,
    "EndAudioTime": 37.45,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "CLINICIAN"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-8",
    "Content": "What does stage mean?",
    "BeginAudioTime": 38.05,
    "EndAudioTime": 39.41,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "PATIENT"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-9",
    "Content": "Staging tells us how deep the tumor goes and whether it's in the lymph nodes or other organs.",
    "BeginAudioTime": 40.01,
    "EndAudioTime": 46.21,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "CLINICIAN"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-10",
    "Content": "The pathologist also described it as moderately differentiated, which means the cells look somewhat abnormal.",
    "BeginAudioTime": 46.81,
    "EndAudioTime": 53.55,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "CLINICIAN"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-11",
    "Content": "Um, and the growth was about 2 centimeters?",
    "BeginAudioTime": 54.15,
    "EndAudioTime": 57.13,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "PATIENT"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-12",
    "Content": "Yes, about 2 centimeters on the scope. We'll also test the tumor for mismatch repair proteins.",
    "BeginAudioTime": 57.73,
    "EndAudioTime": 64.08,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "CLINICIAN"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-13",
    "Content": "Okay. What happens after the scan?",
    "BeginAudioTime": 64.68,
    "EndAudioTime": 67.02,
    "ParticipantDetails": {
     "ParticipantRole": "PATIENT"
    }
   },
   {
    "SegmentId": "seg-14",
    "Content": "We'll meet with surgery and oncology together and go over the options with you.",
    "BeginAudioTime": 67.62,
